            "review_text": "RPascal15\nUnited Kingdom44 contributions\n0\nIt's ok but not very exciting\nMar 2018 • Friends\nWalked past and saw vegetarian so we went in without any preconceptions. \n\nOver ordered (I insisted my 2 choices were enough but my friend encouraged me to get a third!)\n\nCrispy noodles with mixed veg was fabulous, really tasty and fresh, not at all overcooked and featuring a few different mushrooms and some bok choy which was a nice change from the boring cabbage and carrot usually involved.\n\nStir fried morning glory was ok but slightly overcooked.\n\nVegetarian pancake would also have been great but I was stuffed from my noodles! I tried a bit of it and it had various shredded veg and some crushed beans so would have been super filling and balanced meal for a veggie. It's made with egg like a giant omelette so not suitable for vegans.\n\nService was ok but we were sat in Karuna opposite the main restaurant and nobody else in there so there wasn't really any atmosphere.\n\nIt's not a problem that their English is limited so not sure why other reviewers mentioned it, we managed to communicate easily.\n\nFree dessert of fruit salad vovered in condensed milk was a bit random and delivered without ordering. \n\nFor better food at similar prices but limited veggie options you should go to Quan An Ngon in the French quarter. But as this place was closer to our hotel and it was late it was fine on this occasion.\n\nIf you do go to Quan An Ngon don't leave it too late, we sat down at 8:45pm to be told most things had sold out, even all the sticky rice!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 29, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
