            "review_text": "PathManSlough\nSlough, United Kingdom1865 contributions\n0\nFirst evening meal in Vietnam\nJan 2018 • Couples\nMy wife and I ate here on our first night in Hanoi and Vietnam. We were staying just down the street at The Palmy Hotel and wanted a few drinks and something light to eat before bed.\nWe didn't have to even leave the street the hotel is located on before we came across this place. We ordered beer, Gin & tonics (we ended up having 3 G&T's and 2 beers), plus two plates of food, a fried rice dish and a noodle and meat dish. All food was very good.\nThe bill came to about 500K viet dong, which was less than £16 which I thought was good value, given the amount of alcohol we consumed!\nWe returned here for more drinks the following night.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 14, 2018",
